=== HINT 1 ===
Function pointer declaration:
  int (*fn)(int)   - pointer to a function taking int, returning int
Call it like a normal function:  fn(value)

=== HINT 2 ===
Steps inside apply():
  1. malloc a new int array of length len
  2. for each i, set result[i] = fn(arr[i])
  3. return result

=== HINT 3 (SPOILER) ===
int *apply(const int *arr, int len, int (*fn)(int)) {
    int *result = (int *)malloc((size_t)len * sizeof(int));
    if (!result) return NULL;
    for (int i = 0; i < len; i++)
        result[i] = fn(arr[i]);
    return result;
}
